@ 17.7.3.1.3 - Old Norse to Shetland Norn
# citation: Pogostick Man and Marcas Brian MacStiofáin Ó Mhaitiú Ó Domhnaill, from http://nornlanguage.x10.mx/index.php?shet_phon, citing Jakobsen, Jakob, An Etymological Dictionary of the Norn Language NB: For the most part, these changes are not in chronological order and are often tendencies more than strict sound-change laws. Further, I’m assuming that 〈ä〉 is /æ/ and that 〈o̧〉 and 〈ȯ〉 are /ɒ/, and since I’m not sure what the conditions are for (apparent) reflexes with long vowels, I’m ignoring the vowel length in the Shetland Norn reflexes. r alternates with l Final short vowels drop
